The ML-PACE package provides pair styles for machine learning potentials
based on the Atomic Cluster Expansion (ACE) and Graph Atomic Cluster Expansions (GRACE).

It includes the following styles:

1. pair_style pace: An efficient implementation of the standard ACE potential.

2. pair_style grace: Implementation of GRACE models utilizing the TensorFlow
C interface.

3. pair_style grace/fs: A native C++ implementation of GRACE/FS models
(product evaluator) that does not require TensorFlow.

ACE/GRACE is a methodology for deriving a highly accurate classical
potential fit to a large archive of quantum mechanical (DFT) data.

This package was written by Yury Lysogorskiy and others
at ICAMS, the Interdisciplinary Centre for Advanced Materials Simulation,
Ruhr University Bochum, Germany (http://www.icams.de).

Dependencies and Building:

This package requires the external PACE library and, optionally, the
TensorFlow C library (libtensorflow).

When building LAMMPS with CMake, these dependencies are managed automatically:

1. PACE Library: The source code is downloaded and built automatically (via PACELIB_URL or LOCAL_ML-PACE).

2. TensorFlow (for pair_style grace):
  - By default, CMake attempts to locate the TensorFlow C++ library via your Python installation or downloads it automatically.

  - To disable TensorFlow support (and pair_style grace), add `-D NO_GRACE_TF=yes` to your cmake command.

  - To manually specify a TensorFlow library, use -D TF_LIB_FILE=/path/to/libtensorflow_cc.so.

See the LAMMPS manual for more information on building LAMMPS with
external libraries using CMake.

Further Reading:

* ML-PACE implementation source code:
https://github.com/ICAMS/lammps-user-pace
* PACE documentation and model generation tools: https://pacemaker.readthedocs.io
* GRACE documentation and model generation tools: https://gracemaker.readthedocs.io
